    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1126">

                <pb facs="1145" n="859" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg859"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-10-05T19:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 5, 1916, 7 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3899. Department’s instruction 3917, July 17.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d1126-f1"/>
                    Department would be glad to have a confidential report from Hoover as to the recent deportations of
                    civilians from Lille, Roubaix, and Tourcoing; also as to deportations from
                    Belgium, if any, and the present situation.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
